{"parentUuid":"63fadffb-7e9b-4d26-9457-ce94a065db22","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8c799d01-e2bd-4524-a296-769103bb1f55","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ArbN9nPxyyDjsfQqcN6HSW","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough. The reminder doesn't apply — this is a focused review task, not a multi-step implementation. Here's my efficiency review.\n\n# Efficiency Review: feat/entire-why\n\n## High severity\n\n**File: cmd/entire/cli/why_tui.go:296-320 (`renderRows`) — Hot-path bloat**\n\n`renderRows` is called from `refreshViewport()`, which is invoked on every model construction and every `WindowSizeMsg`. It iterates *all* blame rows and runs `highlightWhyCodeLines` on the **entire file** every time, regardless of how many lines fit in the viewport. For a 5000-line file, every resize re-tokenizes/re-formats the whole thing through chroma even though the viewport only shows ~40 rows.\n\n- **Cost**: O(N) chroma tokenization + per-row lipgloss rendering on every resize. Chroma's `Tokenise` + `TTY16m.Format` for thousands of lines is the dominant cost.\n- **Fix**: Cache the rendered row strings (and the highlighted lines) on the model. Only recompute when `m.width` or `data` changes — not when `m.height` or `m.selected` changes. Even better: highlight lazily for visible viewport range only.\n\n**File: cmd/entire/cli/why_tui.go:223-234 (`refreshViewport`) — redundant render of header**\n\n`refreshViewport` calls `m.renderHeader()` and `m.renderColumnHeader()` *just to count newlines* for height math, then `View()` calls them again. With a large blame, `renderHeader` itself is cheap, but doing this on every `WindowSizeMsg` re-runs `renderRows` (the expensive one) via the same path.\n\n- **Fix**: The header is fixed-height (3 lines for header + 1 for column header + 1 footer). Hardcode the constant or compute it once. More importantly, only call `refreshViewport` (which calls `renderRows`) when `width` actually changed; the early-return at line 110 already handles `width==m.width && height==m.height`, but any height-only resize still triggers full re-highlight. Split into `refreshLayout` (cheap, height-only) vs `refreshContent` (expensive, width/data-only).\n\n**File: cmd/entire/cli/why_tui.go:150-164 (`View`) — re-renders every frame**\n\nEach `View()` call rebuilds `renderHeader`, `renderColumnHeader`, `renderViewport`, and `renderFooter`. The viewport's content (highlighted code) is set in `refreshViewport`, so that's cached — good. But up/down arrow keys do not re-call `refreshViewport`, so the hot path here is fine. The header *is* recomputed per frame though, which on selection change is required (it shows the selected row's commit). That's acceptable.\n\n- **Fix (medium)**: Memoize `renderColumnHeader` (depends only on `m.width` and `m.lineWidth`).\n\n## Medium severity\n\n**File: cmd/entire/cli/why_render.go:42 + why_tui.go:323,397 — repeated `plumbing.NewHash` per row**\n\n`renderWhyStatic` and `renderGutter`/`commitInfoForRow` call `plumbing.NewHash(row.CommitHash)` for every blame line on every render. This is a hex-decode per call.\n\n- **Fix**: Store the parsed `plumbing.Hash` on `whyBlameRow` once during `buildWhyBlameRows`, or key `data.Commits` by the string hash to avoid the parse on lookup.\n\n**File: cmd/entire/cli/why_enrich.go:28-60 — sequential commit lookups**\n\nLoops over blame lines, dedupes by hash, calls `repo.CommitObject(hash)` sequentially. For a file blamed across hundreds of unique commits, each is a disk read on the packfile. The dedupe is correct (line 34 skips if already seen).\n\n- **Cost**: N unique commits × commit-object read, sequentially.\n- **Fix**: Run lookups concurrently with a bounded errgroup (e.g., 8–16 workers). Each `CommitObject` is independent and read-only.\n\n**File: cmd/entire/cli/why_highlight.go:34 — full-file join then split**\n\n`strings.Join(lines, \"\\n\")` then `chroma.SplitTokensIntoLines` is fine functionally, but combined with the redundant calls from `renderRows`, this allocates a full file copy per resize. Mitigated entirely by fixing finding #1 (cache).\n\n## Low severity\n\n**File: cmd/entire/cli/why.go:139-150 (`normalizeWhyPathForRel`)** — calls `EvalSymlinks` on both repo root and abs path. Each is one syscall; runs once per invocation. Fine.\n\n**File: cmd/entire/cli/why_tui.go:359-387 (`renderFooter`)** — tries 4 help variants per frame, each calls `lipgloss.Width`. Negligible.\n\n**File: cmd/entire/cli/why_blame.go** — efficient. Single git-blame invocation, single-pass parser, dedupes metadata via `metadataByCommit`.\n\n**File: cmd/entire/cli/why_render.go (static)** — efficient.\n\n## Files efficient as-is\n\n- **why_blame.go**: efficient single-pass parse with metadata dedup.\n- **why_render.go**: only the per-row `plumbing.NewHash` (medium above) is wasteful; otherwise fine for the static path.\n- **why.go**: orchestration only; no redundant work. Git blame runs exactly once.\n\n## Top recommendation\n\nThe biggest win is caching `renderRows()` output (or at least the `highlightWhyCodeLines` result) on `whyTUIModel`, keyed by `(width, colorEnabled)`. Right now any window resize — even a 1-row height change — re-tokenizes the entire file through chroma. For a typical large source file (1k–5k lines) this is the user-visible slowness path."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a6844a1a61b38260b (use SendMessage with to: 'a6844a1a61b38260b' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 55482\ntool_uses: 8\nduration_ms: 56151</usage>"}]}]},"uuid":"8de84d3a-f0c1-4b17-b038-840ead2425c1","timestamp":"2026-05-02T00:00:31.085Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are reviewing a feature branch for **efficiency issues**. The branch `feat/entire-why` adds a new `why` command to the Entire CLI (Go).\n\n## Get the diff\n\nRun: `git diff main...HEAD` from `/Users/pfleidi/entire/cli/.worktrees/feat/entire-why`\n\nFiles changed (new):\n- cmd/entire/cli/why.go