ct(hash)` sequentially. For a file blamed across hundreds of unique commits, each is a disk read on the packfile. The dedupe is correct (line 34 skips if already seen).\n\n- **Cost**: N unique commits × commit-object read, sequentially.\n- **Fix**: Run lookups concurrently with a bounded errgroup (e.g., 8–16 workers). Each `CommitObject` is independent and read-only.\n\n**File: cmd/entire/cli/why_highlight.go:34 — full-file join then split**\n\n`strings.Join(lines, \"\\n\")` then `chroma.SplitTokensIntoLines` is fine functionally, but combined with the redundant calls from `renderRows`, this allocates a full file copy per resize. Mitigated entirely by fixing finding #1 (cache).\n\n## Low severity\n\n**File: cmd/entire/cli/why.go:139-150 (`normalizeWhyPathForRel`)** — calls `EvalSymlinks` on both repo root and abs path. Each is one syscall; runs once per invocation. Fine.\n\n**File: cmd/entire/cli/why_tui.go:359-387 (`renderFooter`)** — tries 4 help variants per frame, each calls `lipgloss.Width`. Negligible.\n\n**File: cmd/entire/cli/why_blame.go** — efficient. Single git-blame invocation, single-pass parser, dedupes metadata via `metadataByCommit`.\n\n**File: cmd/entire/cli/why_render.go (static)** — efficient.\n\n## Files efficient as-is\n\n- **why_blame.go**: efficient single-pass parse with metadata dedup.\n- **why_render.go**: only the per-row `plumbing.NewHash` (medium above) is wasteful; otherwise fine for the static path.\n- **why.go**: orchestration only; no redundant work. Git blame runs exactly once.\n\n## Top recommendation\n\nThe biggest win is caching `renderRows()` output (or at least the `highlightWhyCodeLines` result) on `whyTUIModel`, keyed by `(width, colorEnabled)`. Right now any window resize — even a 1-row height change — re-tokenizes the entire file through chroma. For a typical large source file (1k–5k lines) this is the user-visible slowness path."}],"totalDurationMs":56151,"totalTokens":55482,"totalToolUseCount":8,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,